# Die Spannungsreihe: who takes the electrons, and what a battery is worth
# Part 1 — displacement: a more reactive metal pushes a less reactive one out of solution
register lv1
add v1 water 100mL
add v1 CuSO4 0.01mol
add v1 Mg 0.5g
look v1
measure v1 temp
# Part 2 — the other way round does nothing, and the lab says why
register lv2
new
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 CuSO4 0.01mol
add v2 Ag 0.02mol
# Part 3 — metals and acid: below hydrogen fizzes, above hydrogen sits
new
add v3 water 100mL
add v3 HCl 0.1mol
add v3 Cu 0.02mol
add v3 Mg 0.02mol
# Part 4 — the series as a voltmeter reading: the Daniell cell
new
add v4 water 100mL
add v4 ZnSO4 0.01mol
add v4 Zn 0.05mol
new
add v5 water 100mL
add v5 CuSO4 0.01mol
add v5 Cu 0.05mol
cell v4 v5
# Part 5 — the same cell, ten times less copper: Nernst, over activities
register lv3
new
add v6 water 100mL
add v6 CuSO4 0.001mol
add v6 Cu 0.05mol
cell v4 v6
cell v5 v6
